c6bfccafd897d81d43) in xml_uscAll@119-121.zip","sha256":"c6122974e951003437ece5a998aa7c0b2cdc0f5703dfc78d6135e1fc9e729142","url":"https://uscode.house.gov/download/releasepoints/us/pl/119/121/xml_uscAll@119-121.zip"}},"suggested":false}],"whole_order_end_total":2},"provisional_status":"no","readiness":{"by_step":{"clause_inventory":"confirm","counterevidence":"confirm","ending_or_current_basis":"confirm","opus_media":"n/a","original_text":"confirm","savings_residuals":"agent_judgment","shared_sources":"n/a"},"needs_research":[],"would_satisfy_once_confirmed":["original_text","clause_inventory","ending_or_current_basis","counterevidence"]},"shared_sources":[],"signing_dates_seen":{"fr-originals@jobs/fr-originals/output":"1975-04-01","later-events_catalog":"1975-04-01","stage19_causal_queue":"1975-04-01"},"source_ladder_exhausted_proposed":[],"status":"MACHINE DRAFT - UNVERIFIED; not a claim; see jobs/claim-drafts/AGENT_GUIDE.md"},"claim":{"instrument_id":"EO:11849","later_source_search":[],"operative_clauses":[{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Establishing thie C ollective Bargaining Committee in Construction\nThe President’s Labor-Management Committee established by Execu­\ntive Order No. 11809 was authorized to “encourage the establishment of \nlabor-management committees (bipartite or tripartite) in particular \nsectors or industries as may be appropriate.” That Committee expressed \nthe view that a committee should appropriately be established in the \nconstruction industry.\nAn interim labor-management committee on collective bargaining \nproblems in construction, representative of labor and management orga­\nnizations involved in collective bargaining in the industry, has met reg­\nularly since November 1974 to explore the feasibility and details of a \ncontinuing committee.\nThe recommendations of the interim labor-management committee \nhave been ratified by the standard national labor and management orga­\nnizations engaged in collective bargaining in the industry, and their \nrepresentatives have been authorized to participate and serve cm such a \ncommittee.\nThis Order is required to establish an arrangement and machinery \nfear an operating structure with a minimum of government interference \nin the furtherance of more effective collective bargaining in the industry.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"40 FR 14887, PDF pages 11-12; operative words before the numbered sections","sha256":"8d1e951d0e8c117aea911ab1f0f426f4feb27c442aa99c5becc9557ac2df1d2d","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1975-04-03/pdf/FR-1975-04-03.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11849#preamble-op","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Section 1. There is hereby established the Collective Bargaining Com­\nmittee in Construction (hereinafter referred1  to as the Committee). The \nCommittee shall consist of ten labor members and ten management \nmembers appointed by the President. The Secretary of Labor or his \ndesignee shall serve as Chairman. The Director of the Federal Mediation \nand Conciliation Service shall participate as a member e rf the Committee. \nAdditional alternate members may be appointed by the Secretary of \nLabor.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"40 FR 14887, PDF pages 11-12; Sec. 1","sha256":"8d1e951d0e8c117aea911ab1f0f426f4feb27c442aa99c5becc9557ac2df1d2d","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1975-04-03/pdf/FR-1975-04-03.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11849#sec1","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) The Committee shall facilitate the collective bargaining \nprocess at local and area levels* assist in providing a data bank of wage \nand benefit information* encourage peaceful negotiation of responsible \nlocal and area agreements, facilitate local coordinated bargaining and \nlarger area bargaining wherever appropriate, and seek to resolve par­\nticular disputes that cannot otherwise be reasonably resolved.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"40 FR 14887, PDF pages 11-12; Sec. 2(a)","sha256":"8d1e951d0e8c117aea911ab1f0f426f4feb27c442aa99c5becc9557ac2df1d2d","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1975-04-03/pdf/FR-1975-04-03.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11849#sec2(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) In the furtherance of these objectives the Committee is authorized \nto hold conferences; and if it deems appropriate, in particular collective \nbargaining disputes or in groups of related disputes, the Committee may \nmake recommendations to the appropriate standard organizations which \nare party to collective bargaining in the construction industry concerning \nthe provisions of agreements or the structure of collective bargaining.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"40 FR 14887, PDF pages 11-12; Sec. 2(b)","sha256":"8d1e951d0e8c117aea911ab1f0f426f4feb27c442aa99c5becc9557ac2df1d2d","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1975-04-03/pdf/FR-1975-04-03.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11849#sec2(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(c) The Committee shall promote more effective machinery for the \nresolution of disputes over the terms of collective bargaining agreements\nFEDERAL REGISTER. V O L 40, NO. 65— THURSDAY, APRIL 3, 1975\n\n=== PDF page 12 of 192 ===\n14888 THE PRESIDENT\nwhich recognizes the interests of each branch of the industry and pre­\nserves existing procedures that have been effective.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"40 FR 14887, PDF pages 11-12; Sec. 2(c)","sha256":"8d1e951d0e8c117aea911ab1f0f426f4feb27c442aa99c5becc9557ac2df1d2d","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1975-04-03/pdf/FR-1975-04-03.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11849#sec2(c)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 3. In addition to the foregoing tasks, the Committee shall also:","original_source":{"page_or_item":"40 FR 14887, PDF pages 11-12; Sec. 3 (lead-in)","sha256":"8d1e951d0e8c117aea911ab1f0f426f4feb27c442aa99c5becc9557ac2df1d2d","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1975-04-03/pdf/FR-1975-04-03.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11849#sec3","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) Review and analyze construction manpower under collective \nbargaining agreements, including regional requirements and availabilities \nof respective skills for projected needs, and the effectiveness of training, \nprograms, and, if appropriate, maintain a continuing central data file of \nmanpower requirements and availabilities by major areas of the country;","original_source":{"page_or_item":"40 FR 14887, PDF pages 11-12; Sec. 3(a)","sha256":"8d1e951d0e8c117aea911ab1f0f426f4feb27c442aa99c5becc9557ac2df1d2d","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1975-04-03/pdf/FR-1975-04-03.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11849#sec3(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) Consider measures to reduce the instability of demand for con­\nstruction labor and to provide more weeks of work per year;","original_source":{"page_or_item":"40 FR 14887, PDF pages 11-12; Sec. 3(b)","sha256":"8d1e951d0e8c117aea911ab1f0f426f4feb27c442aa99c5becc9557ac2df1d2d","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1975-04-03/pdf/FR-1975-04-03.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11849#sec3(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(c) Take measures to increase productivity in the industry under col­\nlective bargaining agreements;","original_source":{"page_or_item":"40 FR 14887, PDF pages 11-12; Sec. 3(c)","sha256":"8d1e951d0e8c117aea911ab1f0f426f4feb27c442aa99c5becc9557ac2df1d2d","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1975-04-03/pdf/FR-1975-04-03.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11849#sec3(c)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(d) Improve further the current wage and benefit data base for con­\nstruction to facilitate collective bargaining at local and regional levels and \nthe role of the national organizations in dispute settlements;","original_source":{"page_or_item":"40 FR 14887, PDF pages 11-12; Sec. 3(d)","sha256":"8d1e951d0e8c117aea911ab1f0f426f4feb27c442aa99c5becc9557ac2df1d2d","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1975-04-03/pdf/FR-1975-04-03.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11849#sec3(d)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(e) Consider the problems for collective bargaining arising from the \nactivities of separate Federal government agencies as they affect the con­\nstruction industry;","original_source":{"page_or_item":"40 FR 14887, PDF pages 11-12; Sec. 3(e)","sha256":"8d1e951d0e8c117aea911ab1f0f426f4feb27c442aa99c5becc9557ac2df1d2d","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1975-04-03/pdf/FR-1975-04-03.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11849#sec3(e)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(f) Consider from time to time such problems in the-construction \nindustry under collective bargaining as it may deem appropriate; and","original_source":{"page_or_item":"40 FR 14887, PDF pages 11-12; Sec. 3(f)","sha256":"8d1e951d0e8c117aea911ab1f0f426f4feb27c442aa99c5becc9557ac2df1d2d","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1975-04-03/pdf/FR-1975-04-03.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11849#sec3(f)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(g) Encourage the establishment of comparable joint regional or local \ncommittees on an area basis to the extent it deems appropriate.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"40 FR 14887, PDF pages 11-12; Sec. 3(g)","sha256":"8d1e951d0e8c117aea911ab1f0f426f4feb27c442aa99c5becc9557ac2df1d2d","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1975-04-03/pdf/FR-1975-04-03.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11849#sec3(g)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 4. In carrying out its functions, the Committee shall give con­\nsideration to long term developments in the construction industry under \ncollective bargaining agreements and shall seek to develop appropriate \npolicies in the national interest.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"40 FR 14887, PDF pages 11-12; Sec. 4","sha256":"8d1e951d0e8c117aea911ab1f0f426f4feb27c442aa99c5becc9557ac2df1d2d","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1975-04-03/pdf/FR-1975-04-03.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11849#sec4","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 5. All executive departments and agencies of the Federal govern­\nment are authorized and directed to cooperate with the Committee and \nto furnish such information, personnel and assistance, not inconsistent \nwith law, as it may require in the performance of its duties.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"40 FR 14887, PDF pages 11-12; Sec. 5","sha256":"8d1e951d0e8c117aea911ab1f0f426f4feb27c442aa99c5becc9557ac2df1d2d","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1975-04-03/pdf/FR-1975-04-03.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11849#sec5","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 6. The Committee shall make periodic reports to the President. \nStandard national labor and management organizations are encouraged \nto review the operation of the Committee and report to the President \nannually on the extent to which the purposes of this Order are being \nachieved.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"40 FR 14887, PDF pages 11-12; Sec. 6","sha256":"8d1e951d0e8c117aea911ab1f0f426f4feb27c442aa99c5becc9557ac2df1d2d","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1975-04-03/pdf/FR-1975-04-03.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11849#sec6","state_at_cutoff":null}],"original_representation":{"page_or_item":"40 FR 14887, PDF pages 11-12","sha256":"8d1e951d0e8c117aea911ab1f0f426f4feb27c442aa99c5becc9557ac2df1d2d","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1975-04-03/pdf/FR-1975-04-03.pdf"},"research_rationale":"","savings_residuals":null,"schema":"eo-lifecycle-claim/v1","unresolved_material_gaps":["DRAFT: state_at_cutoff not decided for 16 clause(s); clause inventory completeness not confirmed","DRAFT: whole-order ending not established","DRAFT: savings and residual effects not closed","DRAFT: later_source_search not recorded (machine searches are proposals only; paste them after judging them adequate and resolving every CONFLICT line)"],"whole_order_end":null,"whole_order_status":"no"},"draft_schema":"eo-claim-draft/v1","instrument_id":"EO:11849"}
